{"id": "66816e06-8e79-4d9a-b53b-bf289e06b303", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I recall that in member accounts, calling get-event-selectors with just the trail name for an organization trail fails since it's owned by the management account—you need the full ARN instead. Member accounts can see the org trail via DescribeTrails but can't modify it.

I also need to distinguish management events (bucket-level operations like CreateBucket, PutBucketPolicy) from data events (object-level operations like GetObject, PutObject)—the org trail's HasCustomEventSelectors flag being true just tells me selectors exist, not whether they cover data events specifically. I don't have account access to verify this directly, so I should flag this as something to confirm with the ARN-based lookup rather than guessing.

"}]}
